{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Then he drew near to him: Please, my lord.</b> In the way of the world, one who acquires a slave and he turns out to be a thief returns him — yet this one who turned out to be a thief, you seek for a slave!" "<b>For you are like Pharaoh.</b> Just as Pharaoh desired Sarah our mother on account of her beauty, so you desire Benjamin for a slave on account of his beauty. Another explanation: כי כמוך כפרעה — just as you are great in your place, so we are great in our place."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:03.811266664Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}